    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6143a279-7499-5714-8374-0c28afabefb6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Find all real values of $p$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 - p & 2 p - 7 & p - 4 \\\\ 5 - p & 2 p - 9 & p - 6 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(3 - p)\\begin{vmatrix}2 p - 9 & p - 6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3 - p)((2 p - 9)(2)-(p - 6)(2)) \\\\  & =(3 - p)(2 p - 6) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} + 12 p - 18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(2 p - 7)\\begin{vmatrix}5 - p & p - 6 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2 p - 7)((5 - p)(2)-(p - 6)(-1)) \\\\  & =-(2 p - 7)(4 - p) \\\\  & =2 p^{2} - 15 p + 28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(p - 4)\\begin{vmatrix}5 - p & 2 p - 9 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(p - 4)((5 - p)(2)-(2 p - 9)(-1)) \\\\  & =(p - 4)(1) \\\\  & =p - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =6 - 2 p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 - 2 p & =0 \\\\ - 2 p & =-6 \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=3$.",
